          "en": "You should also add a main header component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.72,
          "end": 17.16,
          "en": "to the page that contains links to the homepage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.16,
          "end": 19.743,
          "en": "and this newly added news page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.79,
          "end": 23.76,
          "en": "So a separate component should be added here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.76,
          "end": 28.76,
          "en": "and I did already mention in the essentials section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.8,
          "end": 30.722,
          "en": "that there will be different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.722,
          "end": 34.2,
          "en": "of structuring your NextJS project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.2,
          "end": 36.24,
          "en": "and that it's up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.24,
          "end": 40.41,
          "en": "where you wanna store component files for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.41,
          "end": 44.37,
          "en": "that you could add a components folder in the app folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.37,
          "end": 46.95,
          "en": "and have your components in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.95,
          "end": 48.45,
          "en": "but that you could for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.45,
          "end": 52.56,
          "en": "also add that components folder outside of the app folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.56,
          "end": 57.48,
          "en": "so as a sibling to the app folder right inside your project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.48,
          "end": 61.02,
          "en": "And all these strategies have different advantages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.02,
          "end": 64.95,
          "en": "and it ultimately comes down to your personal preference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.95,
          "end": 67.41,
          "en": "Now, I will actually store my components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.41,
          "end": 71.28,
          "en": "in a folder outside of the app folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.28,
          "end": 74.91,
          "en": "So I added this components folder as a sibling to app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.91,
          "end": 77.16,
          "en": "and it's in there where I will add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.16,
          "end": 82.16,
          "en": "this main-header.js file where I will export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.68,
          "end": 87.273,
          "en": "this MainHeader component function like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.95,
          "end": 92.58,
          "en": "Well and in there, I will now return a header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.58,
          "end": 95.55,
          "en": "and the goal was to have these links in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.55,
          "end": 98.19,
          "en": "and of course, it's therefor pretty much up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.19,
          "end": 100.35,
          "en": "which mark up you used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.35,
          "end": 103.32,
          "en": "for rendering these two links in the header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.32,
          "end": 106.59,
          "en": "I will add my header like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.59,
          "end": 108.63,
          "en": "and then simply add an unordered list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.63,
          "end": 111.78,
          "en": "with two list items and every list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.78,
          "end": 116.03999999999999,
          "en": "will hold a link using the link component from NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 116.03999999999999,
          "end": 119.1,
          "en": "and on the first link, I'll say home",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.1,
          "end": 121.2,
          "en": "and I'll navigate to /nothing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.2,
          "end": 122.97,
          "en": "because that's the homepage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.97,
          "end": 126.813,
          "en": "and the second link will say News and navigate to /news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.12,
          "end": 132.72,
          "en": "And now we just have to use this MainHeader component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.72,
          "end": 137.04,
          "en": "and we could now manually add it to every page component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.04,
          "end": 141.15,
          "en": "so that it's displayed above the content of that page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.15,
          "end": 144.42000000000002,
          "en": "but that's of course not how you would do it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.42000000000002,
          "end": 147.063,
          "en": "as you learned it in the essentials section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.11,
          "end": 150.54,
          "en": "Instead, in NextJS, you have concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.54,
          "end": 153.84,
          "en": "of working with layouts and pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.84,
          "end": 156.45,
          "en": "and we already saw the idea behind pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.45,
          "end": 158.487,
          "en": "The idea behind layouts is simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.487,
          "end": 162.63,
          "en": "that you create shells around page content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.63,
          "end": 164.97,
          "en": "so that you can have some shared content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.97,
          "end": 167.613,
          "en": "that's the same across multiple pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.48,
          "end": 171.9,
          "en": "And where you create pages with a page.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.9,
          "end": 175.2,
          "en": "you create layouts with a layout.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.2,
          "end": 177.063,
          "en": "That's the idea here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.35,
          "end": 181.5,
          "en": "And therefor, we could create a new layout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.5,
          "end": 184.11,
          "en": "if we wanted to have a news specific layout,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.11,
          "end": 187.59,
          "en": "because you can have nested layouts in NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.59,
          "end": 189.84,
          "en": "but here I actually wanna have a layout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.84,
          "end": 192.15,
          "en": "that spans all my pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.15,
          "end": 195,
          "en": "including the root page, the home page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195,
          "end": 198.54,
          "en": "and hence, I'll go to the root layout.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 198.54,
          "end": 202.38,
          "en": "which exists already, because every NextJS application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.38,
          "end": 205.263,
          "en": "must have such a root layout file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 206.22,
          "end": 208.35,
          "en": "And in that root layout file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 208.35,
          "end": 210.75,
          "en": "I will now go to the body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.75,
          "end": 214.8,
          "en": "which wraps this children output here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 214.8,
          "end": 216.96,
          "en": "which in the end will be the page content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.96,
          "end": 219.39,
          "en": "and above that, I will output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 219.39,
          "end": 222.39,
          "en": "my MainHeader component like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.39,
          "end": 223.95,
          "en": "and of course, for that to work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 223.95,
          "end": 226.98,
          "en": "it must be imported from the MainHeader file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 226.98,
          "end": 228.453,
          "en": "from the components folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 230.43,
          "end": 234.12,
          "en": "And here my IDE added to this import automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.12,
          "end": 236.57999999999998,
          "en": "and it automatically took advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.57999999999998,
          "end": 239.82,
          "en": "of this import path alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.82,
          "end": 242.79,
          "en": "that's supported by NextJS projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.79,
          "end": 247.77,
          "en": "where you can use an at symbol in your file import paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 247.77,
          "end": 250.98,
          "en": "to point at the project root folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 250.98,
          "end": 254.16,
          "en": "and then dive into the different sub-folders from there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.16,
          "end": 256.35,
          "en": "for example, into the components folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 256.35,
          "end": 258.903,
          "en": "which holds that MainHeader component file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 259.92,
          "end": 262.59,
          "en": "And with that, the MainHeader will be output here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.59,
          "end": 267.33,
          "en": "and hence, if we save this, we'll see it up there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.33,
          "end": 270.9,
          "en": "Again, not styled yet, but we'll change this soon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.9,
          "end": 272.43,
          "en": "but I can click these links",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 272.43,
          "end": 275.04,
          "en": "to be taken to the homepage, to the news page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 275.04,
          "end": 277.98,
          "en": "and then we can dive into those detail pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.98,
          "end": 280.38,
          "en": "And that's now all working the way it should",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 280.38,
          "end": 283.47,
          "en": "and we therefor now successfully solved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
